Adoption narrowing mutant m14 (condition 10, system crontabs): the token
check reads only the user field of a job line (the 6th field, or the 2nd
after an @keyword) instead of every token of every non-comment line, so a
line naming the account outside that field, such as an environment-looking
line, passes. Killed by TestRootAdoptedSystemCron (an env-prefix cron.d line
naming the account as its 7th field).

--- a/cmd/swarma-slotd-demo/internal/slotd/adopted_linux.go
+++ b/cmd/swarma-slotd-demo/internal/slotd/adopted_linux.go
@@ -401,7 +401,10 @@
 		if len(fields) == 0 || fields[0][0] == '#' {
 			continue
 		}
-		for _, f := range fields {
+		for i, f := range fields {
+			if i != 5 && (i != 1 || fields[0][0] != '@') {
+				continue
+			}
 			if systemCronToken(f, name, uid) {
 				return fmt.Errorf("line %d names the account: %w", n+1, errSystemCronScheduled)
 			}
